#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114838 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "511342eb-691a-57be-a7cc-f10ab430b575" :question/math-academy-id "e-131" :question/problem "Is the function $y=f(x)$, plotted below, differentiable at $x=-1$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/b9be6cb7e47a4541bf7daca4184816a7.png)" :question/worked-solution "The function $y=f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=-1$.\n\nThe function has a removable discontinuity at $x=-1$. Since it is not continuous at $x=-1$, it is also not differentiable there."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114839 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b4100f8-8a66-5243-b0b6-c36b9d17dac3" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Which Functions are Differentiable at a Given Point From the Function Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "68eb6b1f-955c-550b-9232-3c6115ac220f" :question/math-academy-id "e-132" :question/problem "Which of the following functions are differentiable at the point $x=-1$?\n\n- $f(x) = x^5+1$\n- $g(x) = \\dfrac{2}{x+1}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each function individually.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is a polynomial and is therefore differentiable and continuous for all $x$.\n- The function $g(x)$ has an essential discontinuity at $x=-1$, so it is not differentiable at $x=-1$ either.\n\nIn conclusion, only $f(x)$ is differentiable at the point $x=-1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114840 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable"}] :question/id #uuid "de600cc4-19fc-53a7-babc-fc387eff718c" :question/math-academy-id "e-133" :question/problem "Consider the function $y = f(x)$ whose graph is plotted below. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/e2fa4c174a5001cf56d29ee8a17509dd.png)" :question/worked-solution "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a vertical tangent, so it's not differentiable there.\n- At $x=1$ the function has a cusp, so it's not differentiable there.\n- At $x=2$ the function has a removable discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is not differentiable at $x=0, 1, 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115796 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcbd56f-0fc2-59c5-a016-4272be4734c7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points at Which a Function is Not Differentiable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf6e8497-4669-5084-9732-38c2fbe4d251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47669-a-3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114148} {:answer/id #uuid "d8f2438d-6d60-5115-af40-26ada984c0e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47669-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114149} {:answer/id #uuid "36d333d5-7a67-54ef-91f8-131a778f0daa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47669-a-4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114150} {:answer/id #uuid "4d064a0e-8c94-5a25-be42-711ce4c45961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47669-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114151} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae424b3-cbc6-57db-ad88-a9fc93750070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1691/Source/Images/q-47669-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114152}] :answer-field/correct {:answ